1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,000
f of x is the height, so this is every point on or above the curve.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Boundary first. Factor it to find where it crosses.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
One and two.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Greater than or equal. The curve itself is in the region — solid, never dashed.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Now, which side? The symbol does not tell you. Test a point. Take the origin.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Zero is not greater than two. False — so the origin is out, and you shade the other side.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Here's the trap — 'greater than' does not mean up the page. One test point settles it every time.
